  "about": "Link-key check vectors (PLAN.md, the wire and crypto spec). tagRows: tag = HMAC-SHA256(k, \"floe-kc-v1\" || 0x00 || role || len(roomId) as one byte || roomId || hS || hR), role 0x73 for s and 0x72 for r, k as 22 unpadded base64url characters, hS and hR as hex, the tag as 43 unpadded base64url characters. keyRows: canonical key text (16 bytes; the last character carries 2 data bits, so only A, Q, g, w end a valid key). certRows: real DER certificates with the fingerprint the presenting stack announced in its own SDP; each suite asserts SHA-256(der) equals that fingerprint. Generated by an independent Node script from the formula (records folder tools/gen-keycheck-vectors.mjs), never from the Go or TS code under test; certRows come from a pion dump and a Playwright capture.",
